{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30135 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Tenacissoside B is implicated in the pathogenesis of SN12K1 through a multi-step mechanism involving Prelamin-A/C. The drug targets Prelamin-A/C, which is a key component of the nuclear envelope and plays a role in cell cycle regulation and chromatin structure. Prelamin-A/C is also a target of dipiodialide D, a compound that has been shown to interact with SN12K1. This suggests a potential pathway where Tenacissoside B modulates Prelamin-A/C, which in turn influences SN12K1. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent and robust relationship between Tenacissoside B and SN12K1, with Prelamin-A/C acting as a critical mediator. The high scores from all three paths suggest that the relationship is well-supported by the available data, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance of this interaction.",
